# Third-Party Licenses

This project **does not include** (vendor, bundle or copy) any third-party source code,
container image, model or 3D asset. Everything below is a *referenced* dependency: it is
pulled by Docker or pip from its canonical source, under its own license, when you build the
images or start the simulator, and is listed here so its licensing is visible first.

Versions are the ones pinned in `agent/requirements.lock`, `hud/requirements.lock` and
`host/sim_lib.sh` when this file was generated (2026-10-29). Regenerate it whenever a lock
file or an image digest changes (see "Regenerating this file" at the end).

## Notes that need your attention

* **NVIDIA Isaac Sim is proprietary.** `nvcr.io/nvidia/isaac-sim:6.1.0` (pinned by digest in
  `host/sim_lib.sh`) is distributed by NVIDIA under the NVIDIA Isaac Sim license agreement,
  not an open source license, and the Spot model, the locomotion policy and the other assets
  it loads at run time from NVIDIA's asset server carry NVIDIA's Additional Software and
  Materials License. `host/run_sim.sh` refuses to start until you accept the EULA yourself
  (`ACCEPT_EULA=Y`), and leaves NVIDIA data collection off unless you set `PRIVACY_CONSENT=Y`.
  Read both licenses before you run it:
  https://docs.isaacsim.omniverse.nvidia.com/latest/common/licenses.html
* **The robot vendor.** No vendor software or asset is included or downloaded: the simulated
  Spot comes from NVIDIA's asset library, and the ROS 2 topic names follow the open source
  `spot_ros2` driver so that any ROS 2 robot can publish the same contract. Spot is a
  trademark of Boston Dynamics, Inc., named only to identify that asset.
* **Weak copyleft (MPL-2.0).** `certifi` is MPL-2.0. It is used unmodified as an installed
  package.

